  "equipment_type": "Reverse osmosis water treatment unit BACnet gateway",
  "applies_to": "Condair RO-E and RO-E+ reverse osmosis water treatment units with the optional BACnet IP (2611780) or BACnet MS/TP (2611783) gateway board.",
  "summary": "The Condair RO-E reverse osmosis unit, which feeds water to Condair humidifiers, can be put on BACnet IP or MS/TP with an optional ProtoCessor gateway board. The virtual device reports RO type, operating and service status, capacity, error code, pressures, permeate quality and flow, maintenance hours and valve states, and lets the BMS set the tank pressure band and reset errors.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP",
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": 300,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "These objects belong to the optional gateway board, not the RO-E's BACnet on-board interface; names and instances differ between the two.",
    "Object names are printed with spaces and with the type as a prefix (for example \"MI RO Type\"); AI 106 is printed as AI_ROPermeateConductivity.",
    "Pressure, flow and temperature units follow the Imperial/Metric setting in the RO-E controller.",
    "Conductivity and the drain valve are standard on the RO-E+ and optional on the RO-E; the permeate valve is RO-E+ only; permeate temperature, flow, outlet and concentrate valves are options.",
    "The device table gives instance 300 with a pointer to the gateway configuration section; MS/TP gateways default to Node_ID 1001 there."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "Gateway Board for BACnet and LonWorks - Supplemental Installation and Operation Manual (DL II, ME II, RS II and RO-E)",
    "doc_number": "2603584-F",
    "revision_date": "2026-07",
    "url": "https://www.condair.com/consense/bms-communication-ic-2.0/am_bms_interface_2603584_en.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "The RO-E list is monitoring only, apart from the tank pressure band and an error reset. Map device status, service status and the error code, plus tank and inlet pressure; watch next maintenance and next disinfection for service planning.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AV 103",
        "name": "AV Error/Warning Reset",
        "why": "Reset errors and warnings"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MI 102",
        "name": "MI RO Device Status",
        "why": "Operating status"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 104",
        "name": "AI RO Tank Pressure",
        "why": "Tank pressure"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 103",
        "name": "AI RO Inlet Pressure",
        "why": "Inlet pressure"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 109",
        "name": "AI RO Next Maintenance",
        "why": "Hours to next maintenance"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MI 103",
        "name": "MI RO Service Status",
        "why": "Maintenance/warning/error status"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 101",
        "name": "AI Error Warning Code",
        "why": "Active error/warning code"
      }
    ],
    "enable": null,
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "Gateway BACnet IP defaults to 192.168.1.24/24 on boards built from February 2022 (10.232.72.172/16 before); set it in the FS-GUI web page on port 80.",
      "MS/TP gateways ship as master, MAC 127, 9600 baud, Node_ID (device instance) 1001; change them in the gateway's config.csv.",
      "FS-GUI login is admin plus the password on the board sticker; the manual recommends changing it and switching to HTTPS."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Error codes are listed in the RO-E operation manual, not this addendum.",
      "Pressure, flow and temperature units change with the controller's Imperial/Metric setting."
    ]
  },
